# Yenna, Redtooth Regent: an Aura token with nothing it could legally enchant is not created (CR 303.4g, 111.7). Bot1 plays a Plains and
# enchants it with Consecrate Land ("Enchant land. Enchanted land ... can't be enchanted by other Auras"), and no other land is on the
# battlefield (Bot1's mana comes from Moxen, Bot2 plays nothing). Yenna copies Consecrate Land: the copy could enchant only a land, and
# the one land refuses other Auras, so no token is made. There is no Aura token, so Yenna stays tapped and Bot1 does not scry.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Yenna, Redtooth Regent
Consecrate Land
Plains
Mountain
Forest
Plains x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Yenna, Redtooth Regent.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Consecrate Land.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Plains)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Attached = Consecrate Land > Plains
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Yenna, Redtooth Regent.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Consecrate Land)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Attached = Consecrate Land > Plains
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 7
Bot1.Battlefield.Yenna, Redtooth Regent.Tapped = true
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Library.Count = 12
